  "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nAfter an upgrade from `1.25.0-1~bpo10+1` to `1.26.0-1~bpo10+1`, synapse failed to start with:\r\n2021-02-04 19:30:11,914 - synapse.config.appservice - 90 - ERROR - None- Failed to load appservice from '/home/matrix-irc/matrix-appservice-irc/my_registration_file.yaml'\r\n2021-02-04 19:30:11,914 - synapse.config.appservice - 91 - ERROR - None- [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/home/matrix-irc/matrix-appservice-irc/my_registration_file.yaml'\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/synapse/config/appservice.py\", line 67, in load_appservices\r\n    with open(config_file, \"r\") as f:\r\nPermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/home/matrix-irc/matrix-appservice-irc/my_registration_file.yaml'\r\n\r\nThe matrix-synapse user which is used to run synapse has access to that file, it wouldn't have worked with a previous version if it didn't. I've moved the file to /etc/matrix-synapse/ with the same permissions, and now it works.\r\n\r\nIs this some security feature that was added?",
